        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): bound one-shot WebClient/write timeouts without Bolt deadline",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`@slack/web-api` defaults `timeout` to `0` (no deadline). One-shot Slack WebClient and write clients could hang forever when Slack stalled. Lookup already defaulted to 30s; web/write did not.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPrior tip failed CI for two reasons:\n\n1. **Knip** — public `SLACK_*_TIMEOUT_MS` exports with no production callers\n2. **Bolt contamination** — `provider.ts` passes `resolveSlackWebClientOptions()` into `createSlackBoltApp`. A default timeout on that shared resolver gives Bolt's long-lived client a request deadline\n\n**Fix shape (Bolt-safe):**\n- `resolveSlackWebClientOptions` stays **timeout-free** (Bolt / Socket Mode)\n- `createSlackWebClient` applies a private **30s** one-shot deadline\n- `resolveSlackWriteClientOptions` applies a private **60s** write deadline (`??=`)\n- No new public timeout constant exports\n- Whole-path stalled-header proofs live in `client.web-api.test.ts` (real `@slack/web-api` + local server; `client.test.ts` mocks `WebClient` so cannot own hang proof)\n\n## User Impact\n\n- One-shot Slack API calls get bounded timeouts\n- Bolt / Socket Mode listener path unchanged\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Head SHA:** `f5204c7af79d4c1cf9ff36d8b38f518360370f28`\n**Base:** `59fa034fcbcbe1a44b16e864c667077f5b1c35db`\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Files / net | 4 files, +109 / -1 (4th file = real Web API hang proof; mocked client tests cannot cover abort) |\n| Knip | no public `SLACK_*_TIMEOUT_MS` exports |\n| Bolt | `resolveSlackWebClientOptions().timeout` stays undefined |\n| One-shot web default | `createSlackWebClient` → timeout 30000 |\n| Write default | `resolveSlackWriteClientOptions` → timeout 60000 |\n| L2/L3 hang | stalled-header local Slack API server; createSlackWebClient / createSlackWriteClient abort; proof lines include host/pid/ts |\n\n### L3 runtime transcript\n\nWill append CI / local vitest lines matching `[slack one-shot web stall proof]` and `[slack write stall proof]` for this head once the focused web-api shard prints them.\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
